==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|THREE THERE WERE WHO MADE THE JOURNEY, WITHOUT WHOSE KNOWLEDGE THERE IS NO RETURNING&hellip;A PATHWAY CONNECTING NEAR AND FAR, ACROSS THE HEAVENS STAR TO STAR&hellip;DESPITE GREAT POWERS WHICH DO OBJECT, THIS SECRET WAY THE THREE PROTECT&hellip;SO HEED THE PATH WITH A WATCHFUL EYE, FOR IF YOU WANDER YOU WILL DIE&hellip;|A fan translation of the [[Unidentified runic alphabet|runes]]|<ref name="JCF">{{JCFCite|url=posts/58683147|board=Literature|thread=The Essential Atlas and Galactic Cartography: Official Discussion|user=[[Jason Fry|jasonfry]]|date=2023-10-28|time=5:22 PM|quote=Different planets with same name.|archivedate=20231029035113}}</ref>}}
The Nightsisters' Temple first appeared in "[[Part One: Master and Apprentice]]," the first episode of the live-action [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]'',<ref name="Part One" /> which was released on [[August 22]], [[2023]].<ref name="New Release Date">{{SW|url=news/ahsoka-new-premiere-date|text=''Ahsoka'' Premiere Moves Up to Tuesday, August 22|date=2023-08-18|quote=The two-episode premiere of ''Ahsoka'' will now arrive on Tuesday, August 22 at 6 p.m. PT on Disney+}}</ref> However, the stronghold was never identified until it's very own [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry was added.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|nightsisters-temple-on-arcana|Nightsisters' Temple on Arcana}}</ref>

[[Frances Lebar]], the art director of the series later released multiple production photos of the set design,<ref name="Frances Lebar">{{WebCite|url=https://www.franceslebar.com/ahsoka|text=Arcana behind-the-scenes production photos|author=[[Frances Lebar]]|date=2023-10-29|archivedate=20231029041319}}</ref> allowing fans to translate the runes written around the temple.<ref name="JCF" />

